  "note": "Urban district election, 17 May 1961; two wards, 15 seats (5 East, 10 West). The East Ward was returned unopposed (Banbridge Chronicle, 5 May 1961, p. 1). Eleven candidates for the ten West Ward seats. The sitting member Mr. Samuel McMillan was defeated; no vote is printed for him, so he is recorded without one. Electorate 2,065; 638 voted.",
